{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "parent": "AUTH-TENANT-BLOCKING",
  "parentStatus": "IMPLEMENTING",
  "oracleTrack": "disposable-sandbox",
  "scopeDecisions": [
    {
      "id": "TB1",
      "decision": "Blocking functions are observed on the Identity Platform sandbox: Cloud Functions (2nd gen), Cloud Build, Artifact Registry, Cloud Run and Eventarc are enabled there; per recording one blocking-function fixture is deployed and registered, and at the end and on every stop path it is unregistered and its function, image and source are deleted and read back. allUsers invoker only for a fixture without side effects or secrets, about an hour per recording, removed afterwards and read back in the pre-send review. Budget US$10 per observation task.",
      "decidedBy": "owner (t-k)",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-25"
    },
    {
      "id": "TB2",
      "decision": "Per program the sandbox's multiTenant.allowTenants is switched on, the program's tenants (unique display names) are created and their settings switched, and at the end and on every stop path the tenants are deleted, allowTenants is switched off, and both are read back. Project settings a program changes to compare inheritance (T7) are restored and read back the same way. No overlap with FS-RULES on the sandbox.",
      "decidedBy": "owner (t-k); the T7 project settings confirmed in scope by Claude under the owner's delegation",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-25"
    },
    {
      "id": "TB3",
      "decision": "beforeSendEmail and beforeSendSms are in scope. Whether beforeSendSms fires for a configured test phone number is checked once; if it does not, it is recorded as unobserved.",
      "decidedBy": "owner (t-k)",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-25"
    },
    {
      "id": "TB4",
      "decision": "Out of scope: the content of OIDC and SAML providers and identity-provider sign-in in a tenant (AUTH-FEDERATION; provider configurations staying inside their tenant is in scope), the SDK paths (AUTH-CONFIG-SDK), reCAPTCHA enforcement, the delivery of real mail and SMS, and the effect of monitoring settings (they are only read and written).",
      "decidedBy": "owner (t-k)",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-25",
      "movedTo": "AUTH-FEDERATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "TB5",
      "decision": "A blocking event is compared as the decoded event the function receives. The event JWT itself (signed with Google's keys) is a documented divergence: fireemu delivers the decoded event to its runner.",
      "decidedBy": "owner (t-k)",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-25"
    },
    {
      "id": "TB6",
      "decision": "Blocking functions are observed with 2nd gen functions and the current firebase-functions; only if production refuses the 2nd gen event audience again is the observation switched to 1st gen, after telling the coordinator, and the 2nd gen refusal is recorded as an observation.",
      "decidedBy": "Claude under the owner's delegation (agent decision)",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-25"
    },
    {
      "id": "TB7",
      "decision": "Custom tokens with a tenant_id are minted through the time-limited signJwt-only binding already approved for AUTH-CREDENTIAL, AUTH-MFA (M5) and FS-RULES, only while a recording runs and never overlapping another lane's binding; granting and removing it is recorded and read back in the pre-send review.",
      "decidedBy": "Claude under the owner's delegation",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-25"
    },
    {
      "id": "TB8",
      "decision": "The project config shape, multiTenant included, is AUTH-CONFIG-SDK's. After AUTH-CONFIG-SDK closes, work/auth-config-sdk is merged here and the allowTenants enforcement is added on top (strict refuses tenant operations while it is off, as production does; the emulator profile adds no refusal). Until then local rows that need the switch are pending integration.",
      "decidedBy": "Claude under the owner's delegation",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-25"
    },
    {
      "id": "M2",
      "decision": "Multi-factor configuration per tenant and every tenant/MFA interaction moved here from AUTH-MFA.",
      "decidedBy": "owner (t-k)",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-25"
    },
    {
      "id": "M6",
      "decision": "Blocking functions that see a second factor moved here from AUTH-MFA.",
      "decidedBy": "owner (t-k)",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-25"
    },
    {
      "id": "E4",
      "decision": "Action codes in tenants and around blocking functions moved here from AUTH-ACTION.",
      "decidedBy": "owner (t-k)",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-24"
    },
    {
      "id": "A12",
      "decision": "The gson parser message production returns for malformed customAttributes JSON is a documented message-text divergence; the INVALID_CLAIMS refusal itself must match.",
      "decidedBy": "owner",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-24",
      "inheritedFrom": "AUTH-ACCOUNT"
    },
    {
      "id": "TB9",
      "decision": "The emulator profile's blocking-function error and timeout texts follow production's form (no new refusal); the masked 503 Error code: 47 and a failure while the runner restarts are defects in both profiles.",
      "decidedBy": "Claude under the owner's delegation to the coordinator (owner ledger, 2026-09-28, AUTH-TENANT-BLOCKING)",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-28"
    },
    {
      "id": "TB10",
      "decision": "beforeEmailSent (B6) and production's blockingFunctions answer (B7) are implemented in the strict profile only: the emulator profile runs no email or SMS event and keeps its own configuration form, as the official emulator does; every mail path reaches one check; beforeSmsSent is listed and never run (no SMS it would gate is recorded, TB3). The strict profile's race guards (409) are fireemu-only and recorded in the contract.",
      "decidedBy": "Claude under the owner's delegation to the coordinator (owner ledger, 2026-09-28, AUTH-TENANT-BLOCKING)",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-28"
    },
    {
      "id": "TB11",
      "decision": "Two recorded rows are compared again on the integrated artifact instead of being implemented here: atb/tenant/providers#auth-uri-a (AUTH-FEDERATION, TB4) and atb/blocking/timeout#sign-in-slow (FUNCTIONS-HTTP's runner recovery). The lane is integrated after v0.8.0 and before AUTH-FEDERATION.",
      "decidedBy": "Claude under the owner's delegation to the coordinator (owner ledger, 2026-09-28, AUTH-TENANT-BLOCKING)",
      "decidedOn": "2026-09-28"
    }
  ],
